      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2521017595,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This isn't necessary, you can accomplish this already with the `vals` [display filter function](display filter function):\n\n```\nvals(diameter.applicationId) contains \"S6\"\nvals(diameter.cmd.code) contains \"Auth\"\n```\n\nYou don't need the `vals` function at all if you're just matching the string, i.e. `diameter.applicationId == \"3GPP S6a/S6d\"`, works, but the contains and matches functions require hinting that it should be transformed to the value string first.\n\nIt might be a worthwhile enhancement to the display filter logic to also implicitly convert to the value string for contains and matches.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
